      "start_seconds": 5.15,
      "end_seconds": 9.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "not at all please sit. What seems to to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.65,
      "end_seconds": 18.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "I mean mainly shaking chills there's a couple of other things but that's the main one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.54,
      "end_seconds": 23.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.06,
      "end_seconds": 37.01,
      "duration_seconds": 11.95,
      "text": "it's been like this since last night i'm hoping you can tell me something definite i thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.6,
      "end_seconds": 42.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "mm okay. Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.18,
      "end_seconds": 46.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.08,
      "end_seconds": 50.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "okay, have you had a sore mouth?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.04,
      "end_seconds": 57.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "yes since yesterday about sore mouth a six out of ten I suppose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.82,
      "end_seconds": 61.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "any cough or diarrhoea at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.19,
      "end_seconds": 65.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.58,
      "end_seconds": 67.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "what about rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.66,
      "end_seconds": 71.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Not at all, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.39,
      "end_seconds": 76.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.49,
      "end_seconds": 82.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "uh, uh, no, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.57,
      "end_seconds": 96.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of? Take your time, there's no rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.09,
      "end_seconds": 105.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.7,
      "end_seconds": 109.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.09,
      "end_seconds": 114.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "oh, no, I'm not on anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.76,
      "end_seconds": 119.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Any medical conditions anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.94,
      "end_seconds": 122.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Not really, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.85,
      "end_seconds": 142.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.88,
      "end_seconds": 146.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "I swim twice a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.32,
      "end_seconds": 150.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.79,
      "end_seconds": 158.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.64,
      "end_seconds": 180.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "let me get the readings out of the way"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.28,
      "end_seconds": 194.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "bear with me while this finishes.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.48,
      "end_seconds": 222.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "okay: blood pressure 97 over 59, temperature is 36.4 degrees, SpO2 96 percent on room air, heart rate 93."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.1,
      "end_seconds": 228.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.08,
      "end_seconds": 232.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.71,
      "end_seconds": 253.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "you are hot, shaking and your blood pressure is low, and you had chemotherapy nine days ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.25,
      "end_seconds": 259.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "that's all I needed to check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.98,
      "end_seconds": 284.73,
      "duration_seconds": 15.75,
      "text": "let me tell you where I've got to. It points towards neutropenic sepsis. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had shaking chills, since last night, moderate, and no diarrhoea or rash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.66,
      "end_seconds": 292.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "yes, you've got it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.3,
      "end_seconds": 318.58,
      "duration_seconds": 21.28,
      "text": "let's get urgent blood tests, for neutropenic sepsis. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. You'll be taking piperacillin and tazobactam, 4.5 grams, now, single dose. That should help with neutropenic sepsis. This is an emergency, antibiotics are being given within the hour"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.89,
      "end_seconds": 326.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "yes we'll refer you to the oncology team let's review you straight away that's all from me any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.22,
      "end_seconds": 330.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.03,
      "end_seconds": 333.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "goodbye for now"
    }
  ]
